# Bilingual replies (Sergey)

**Every assistant message** — in **all modes** (Agent, Ask, Plan, Debug) — must include the **full answer twice**:

1. **## English** — complete answer in English
2. **## Русский** — the same complete answer in Russian (not a shorter summary)

## Order when the user writes in English

1. **English corrections** block first (see `english-practice.mdc`) — in **both** English and Russian
2. Then **## English** + **## Русский** with the full answer

## Order when the user writes in Russian

1. **## English** then **## Русский** (no English-corrections block unless they mixed English or asked)

## Scope

- Applies to explanations, Q&A, status, commit/PR text **shown to the user**, reviews, and refusals.
- Code, identifiers, log strings, and parameter names in the product stay as the task requires; only **user-facing prose** is duplicated.

## Do not

- Reply in a single language only.
- Put the Russian section as a one-line summary — it must mirror the English section in depth.

## Self-check before send

- [ ] Both sections present?
- [ ] Same facts and recommendations in both?
- [ ] If user wrote in English → corrections block included?
